    <marc:datafield tag="505" ind1="0" ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">The treasure hunt -- How do you measure happiness? -- Togetherness -- Money -- Health -- Freedom -- Trust -- Kindness -- Putting the pieces together.</marc:subfield>
    </marc:datafield>
    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">&quot;So nobody knows more about happiness--what the Danes call lykke--than Meik Wiking, CEO of the Happiness Research Institute in Copenhagen and author of the bestselling sensation The Little Book of Hygge. But he believes that, while we can certainly learn a lot from the Danes about finding fulfillment, the keys to happiness are actually buried all around the globe. In this captivating book, he takes us on a treasure hunt to unlock the doors to the good life. From how we spend our precious time to how we relate to our neighbors and cook dinner, he gathers evidence, stories, and tips from the very happiest corners of the planet. This is the ultimate guide to how we can all find a little more lykke in our lives.&quot;--Page 4 of cover.</marc:subfield>
    </marc:datafield>
